6. The Reader Interface

STRATA should render at least four synchronized views.

A. Fluent

Readable English optimized for literary force.

B. Glass

Closer-to-source English preserving unusual structure.

C. X-Ray

Interlinear tokens, lemma, morphology, glosses, syntax, and alternatives.

D. Stratigraphy

Footnotes showing semantic history, rhetorical layers, ambiguities, variants,
and interpretive forks.

Example conceptual UI:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ORIGINAL                                    │
│ [token] [token] [token] ...                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ FLUENT                                      │
│ readable literary English                   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ GLASS                                       │
│ near-source structural English              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ LAYERS                                      │
│ ① lexical ambiguity                         │
│ ② root echo                                 │
│ ③ syntax permits alternate attachment       │
│ ④ sound pattern disappears in English       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ READING LATTICE                             │
│         ┌─ reading A                         │
│ source ─┼─ reading B                         │
│         └─ reading C                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

The reader can choose what degree of compression they want.

