7. Multilingual Corpus Adapters

The engine is corpus-agnostic. Adapters normalize external resources into the same schema.

Useful existing building blocks include:

• Morphologically annotated Greek New Testament datasets.
• Linguistically annotated Hebrew Bible datasets.
• Qur’anic Arabic morphology/syntax corpora.
• Classical Syriac digital corpora.
• Historical lexica, critical apparatuses, manuscript witnesses, and parallel corpora.

Adapters should never silently mix textual traditions.
For example, Greek New Testament, Syriac Peshitta, Hebrew Bible, and later translations
are distinct witnesses/interfaces and should be compared rather than conflated.

Canonical adapter output:

```json
{
  "text_id": "work.book.section",
  "language": "grc",
  "date_range": [-100, 200],
  "witness": "named textual witness",
  "tokens": [
    {
      "surface": "...",
      "lemma": "...",
      "morphology": {},
      "glosses": [],
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
  "syntax": [],
  "variants": [],
  "provenance": []
}
```

