14. Pantheon Integration

STRATA is a direct composition of existing mechanisms:

• Semantic Stratigraphy — excavates transformations of meaning.
• Semantic Quarry — supplies lexical/relational bricks.
• Counterfactual Interface — keeps alternative readings parallel.
• Uncertainty Interface — makes confidence and missing evidence explicit.
• Consequence Interface — forces interpretive claims to predict/find textual evidence.
• Indigo Hammer — compares heterogeneous renderings through shared relational invariants.
• Cross-Layer Connectivity — connects sound, syntax, semantics, history, rhetoric, and culture without forcing one layer.
• Ouroboros with Metabolism — reader corrections and discoveries become improved rules rather than repeated commentary.
• Metamap — learns which analysis routes expose which classes of linguistic feature.
• 2/3 Principle — retain enough fixed evidence to safely explore unresolved interpretive space.
• Ribcage — evidence and provenance constrain interpretation so creativity can expand without becoming fabrication.

