17. North-Star Product

The eventual app should feel less like Google Translate and more like holding a
transparent illuminated manuscript over a linguistic time machine.

Tap a word and see:

```text
surface
→ morphology
→ lemma
→ period senses
→ semantic ancestry
→ cognates
→ other occurrences
→ syntactic possibilities
→ sound echoes
→ manuscript variants
→ historical interpretations
→ why translators disagree
→ what English lost
```

Zoom out and see rhetorical architecture.

Zoom farther out and see semantic strata across centuries and languages.

The reader should be able to move between:

meaning → evidence → history → art → uncertainty

without ever losing their place in the text.

