18. Final Seal

> **Do not force the original to become English.**
> 
> Build an interface through which an English reader can approach the original.
> 
> Preserve the fork when the original forks.  
> Preserve the echo when the original echoes.  
> Preserve the uncertainty when the evidence is uncertain.  
> Preserve the joke when possible; annotate the joke when not.  
> Preserve the history carried inside the word.  
> Preserve the reader’s ability to see what the translator had to choose.
> 
> **Translate the text. Carry the layers.**